<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 258 0 R/E(The StudAI Foundry Hackathon served as a competitive platform for developing advanced AI-driven solutions addressing real-world industrial challenges. In this event, the team presented \215Foundry Brain,\216 an autonomous AI agent designed to optimize foundry operations through intelligent scheduling and defect analysis.)/Pg 50 0 R/K[15]>>
endobj

948 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 258 0 R/E(The system focuses on automating casting order processing, furnace scheduling, and quality assurance using AI-based decision-making. It integrates constraint-based scheduling, retrieval-augmented generation \(RAG\), and self-correcting mechanisms to ensure efficient and reliable operations in manufacturing environments.)/Pg 50 0 R/K[16]>>
endobj

949 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 258 0 R/E(As described in the project \(Track 3: Autonomous Workflow & Operations Systems\), the solution is capable of processing orders, scheduling furnace slots, detecting defects, and generating audit reports autonomously with minimal human intervention .)/Pg 50 0 R/K[17]>>
endobj

